 "name": "Rural Street Design: Emotional Evaluation",
 "description": "Faithful replication with the paper's own stimuli: participants give gender, age range and education, then see six SketchUp/Lumion design renderings of village streets in Huixingtou Village, Handan (two schemes each for a main road, a side road and a front-of-house road). Each rendering follows a 10 s fixation cross and is shown for 10 s; participants then rate it on the paper's six 5-point bipolar items: scale, aesthetics, publicness, lingering, enjoyment and security. Rebuilt from Wang, Yang & Wang (2025), PLOS ONE 20(6): e0326049, with the renderings printed in the paper's Figure 2 and the items of its Table 2 (CC BY 4.0). Analysis as in the paper: Cronbach's alpha of the six items; Kruskal-Wallis tests across the three street scales; compare the six designs item by item (ANOVA with LSD post-hoc). Differences from the original study: (1) the original was a lab eye-tracking study (aSee Pro, 27-inch screen); this web version records no gaze, pupil or saccade data; (2) the renderings are cropped from the published figure, so they are smaller (about 335 px wide) than the 1920 x 1080 originals; (3) the paper does not say whether the order was randomised; here the six renderings appear in random order; (4) the answer options for age range and education are our wording, since the paper names these questions but does not print the options; (5) no 60 s time limit on the ratings.",
